    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15493" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρρεπής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, of a
		balance, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>inclining to neither
				side</i>: hence, <i>without weight</i> or <i>influence,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρρεπὲς πρὸς εὐδαιμονίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.1070a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1015a
			</span></i>; <i>insignificant,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Stoic.
				3.35
			</span></i>; <i>firm, unwavering,</i> of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσότης,</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				159
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				283
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.409
				</span></i>
			, Hierocl.<i><span class="en">
				p.31
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρρεν-πί</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				<u>Epim.</u>
				256
			</span></i>.</div>
